[52.490179, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m\u258e\u001b[5G\u001b[22m\u001b[3msplit row-wise? I need to rule out cross-split leakage before I start training. Thanks!\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1m\ud83d\udce5 alice\u001b[22m \u00b7 now\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[2m\u258e\u001b[22m \u001b[3mv3 is row-wise random split (70/15/15), NOT grouped by customer_id \u2014 same customer can appear in\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[2m\u258e\u001b[5G\u001b[22m\u001b[3mtrain/val/test, so it leaks for per-customer models. Use customer-churn-v3.1 instead: same \r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bschema/rows but GroupShuffleSplit on customer_id (70/15/15), no customer cro\u001b[82Gses splits.\u001b[23m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1m\ud83d\udce4 you\u001b[22m \u00b7 now\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[2m\u258e\u001b[22m \u001b[3mThanks for the quick check \u2014 since v3 is row-wise and leaks per-customer, I'll switch to \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[2m\u258e\u001b[5G\u001b[22m\u001b[3mcustomer-churn-v3.1 (grouped by customer_id) for training.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BConfirmed with alice: \u001b[1mv3 leaks\u001b[22m (row-wise split), so use \u001b[1mcustomer-churn-v3.1\u001b[79G\u001b[22m(grouped\u001b[88Gby\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcustomer_id)\u001b[16Ginstead.\u001b[25GWrapped\u001b[33Gup\u001b[36G\u2014\u001b[38Gwake\u001b[43Gmonitor\u001b"]
[52.490317, "o", "[51Gstays\u001b[57Garmed\u001b[63Gfor\u001b[67Ganything\u001b[76Gfurther.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m\u273b\u001b[3GSaut\u00e9ed for 9s \u00b7 2 monitors still running\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;5;231m\u25cf\u001b[3G\u001b[39mMonitor event: \"wake on alice's reply to bob's\u001b[50Ginbox\"\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
