[52.972146, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G\u001b[2m\u258e\u001b[5G\u001b[22m\u001b[3msplit row-wise? I need to rule out cross-split leakage before I start training. Thanks!\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1m\ud83d\udce5 alice\u001b[12G\u001b[22m\u00b7\u001b[14Gnow\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[3mv3 \u001b[9Gs row-wi\u001b[18Ge random\u001b[27Gsplit\u001b[33G(70/15/15), NOT gr\u001b[52Guped by customer_id \u2014 same customer can \u001b[93Gppear in\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Btrain/val/test,\u001b[21Gso it leaks for per-customer mo\u001b[53Gels. Use customer-churn-v3.1 in\u001b[85Gtead: \u001b[92Game \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[2m\u258e\u001b[5G\u001b[22m\u001b[3mschema/rows but GroupShuffleSplit on customer_id (70/15/15), no customer crosses splits.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1m\ud83d\udce4 you\u001b[10G\u001b[22m\u00b7\u001b[12Gnow\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[3mThanks for the quick check \u2014\u001b[34Gsin\u001b[38Ge v3 is row-wise and leaks per-customer, I'll switch to \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[2m\u258e\u001b[5G\u001b[22m\u001b[3mcustomer-churn-v3.1 (grouped by customer_id) for training.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BConfirmed with alice:\u001b[25G\u001b[1mv3 leaks\u001b[22m (row-wise split), so use \u001b[1mcustomer-churn-v3.1\u001b[22m (grouped\u001b[88Gby\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcustomer_id)\u001b[16Ginstead.\u001b[25GWrapped\u001b"]
